    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d387">

                <pb facs="0772" n="652" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg652"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.30/63: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crosby</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-07-24T12:00:00-03:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 24,
                                1922—12 noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 4:05
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>76. My 75 July 22, 12 noon.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d387-f1"/> Following is
                    translation of note I have just received from Minister of Marine: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I have the honor to inform Your Excellency that the Brazilian Government
                            has decided to authorize the contracting of a North American naval
                            mission and that the necessary steps have already been taken by the
                            Ministry of Foreign Affairs in order that negotiations can be opened.
                            The Government and the Ministry of Marine desire that the mission be
                            headed by the distinguished Admiral Vogelgesang.”<anchor n="4"
                                xml:id="d387-f2"/></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>As President, press and public are anxious to have Vogelgesang head mission I
                    hope his nomination may be made at earliest possible <pb facs="0773" n="653"
                        xml:id="pg653"/> moment and that he be instructed to come to Rio immediately
                    upon receipt of official Brazilian request for mission which is being
                    transmitted through Embassy at Washington.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crosby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d387-f1" n="3" xml:id="d387-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d387-f2" n="4" xml:id="d387-f2-content">
                <p>The Navy Department announced, July 12, 1922, that Captain Vogelgesang had been
                    recommended by the Naval Selection Board for promotion to the rank of rear
                    admiral; the promotion became effective Oct. 15, 1922.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
